nova-sprint: a sprint of work cards, dealt to a fleet of workers and read before they land

One store holds the cards. Each tick deals ready cards to workers (fleet members and friends),
asks readers to read the finished work and queues what passed to land. What the machine cannot
decide goes to the coordinator's inbox as a judgment that prints the commands answering it.
Who reads what: the coordinator, every group; a worker, "work rows"; a reader, "reads and
review"; a friend, "friends"; the fleet's admin, "fleet and readers", "machines and the store".
Start here: where (the sprint now), inbox (what needs you), help playbook (what to do when).
The law: the tools do the mechanical work. Find the verb first; never do a verb's work by hand.

look at the sprint:
  where [--watch] [--all] [--json]               the sprint now: machine, tables, rows and ETA
  inbox [--wait] [--open <group>]                the judgments waiting on you, each with its answers
  view coordinator [--all] [--json]              everything that needs the seat, in one read
  view cards [--col <c>] [--by tier|stream]      list or count the cards by column, stream or holder
  view worker --as <member|friend>               one worker's cards, packets and results not landed
  card <id> [--brief | --fields]                 one card: its brief, attempts, state and log
  streams [--cards] [--release <name>]           each stream: repositories, bases, open and landed
  needs [--stream <s>] [--roots]                 the waiting cards and the needs they wait on
  held [--stream <s>]                            the held cards
  sentinels [--stream <s>]                       the sentinels and what each one waits on
  bases                                          each base the open cards name: ahead, behind, gate
  log [--card <id>] [--since <10m>]              the sprint's change log
  stats [--routes]                               the sprint's counts and rates
  rules                                          what the tick's rules would answer, and why idle
  handover                                       what the next holder of the seat needs
  dashboard [--listen <addr:port>]               serve the sprint's web page and pull routes

run the machine:
  init [--readers <a,b>] [--members <m:width>]   create the sprint: readers, members, coordinator
  start                                          start the machine ticking
  stop --reason <text> --until <time>            stop the machine until the next start
  run [--listen <addr:port>] [--land]            the server loop: tick, serve the verbs, land
  tick [--shadow]                                one tick by hand: deal, ask reads, queue merges
  resolve [<id>...] [--stream <s>]               move waiting cards whose needs landed to ready
  watch --wake [--every <duration>]              block until something needs the coordinator
  remind --in <duration> --note <text>           a timer that wakes its actor as a judgment
  play [--seed <n>] [--every <duration>]         simulate the world outside the tables on a twin
  quack --streams <a,b> --repo <clone url>       add the end-to-end test cards, --count per stream
  selftest [--dir <d>] [--keep]                  run the card flow on a scratch twin and repository
  selftest land [--binary <path>]                land a canned card on a scratch clone
  clear --confirm sprint                         a new epoch, every setting at its working default
  teardown --confirm sprint                      delete the sprint's records from the store

cards and briefs:
  add --stream <s> --brief-file <f>...           admit cards (or <id>..., --brief-dir, --count)
  preflight --brief-dir <dir>                    check a directory of briefs before adding it
  brief check <file|dir>... [--stream <s>]       every check add runs, over briefs; writes nothing
  check cards [--stream <s>...] [--dry-run]      the card check before start, recorded for start
  brief <id> --brief-file <path>                 re-brief a card in place (or --tier, --widen)
  recut <id> (--tier <t> | --brief-file <f>)     re-cut a card as its twin
  twin <card> [--paths <p,...>] [--carry]        replace a card by its twin, widened
  relink <old-id>[,<old-id>] <new-id>            re-point what waited on old cards to their twin
  continue <card> --note <text>                  carry a bound card's pushed work to a next attempt
  tier <card> --set <tier> --reason <text>       set a card's tier without editing its brief
  move <id>... --stream <s>                      move cards to another stream
  rank <id>... (--first | --score <n>)           change cards' place in their stream
  priority <id>... --high --reason <text>        set cards' priority, blocker down to low
  unpin <id>... --reason <text>                  take the WHO pin off unstarted cards
  sentinel set <id> --needs <a,b>                replace a sentinel's needs
  card base <id> <branch>                        point a merging card at another base on origin
  rebase --from <branch> --to <branch>           move every unlanded card from one base to another
  drop <id>... --reason <text>                   drop cards; they are never dealt again
  defer <id>... --repo-dir <dir>                 write waiting cards to the roadmap, then drop them

answer the inbox:
  accept (<id>... | --group <id> --expect <n>)   move passed cards in review to the merge queue
  rework <id>... --fix <text>                    open the cards' next attempt with what to fix
  return <id>... --reason <text>                 take merging cards off the queue, back to review
  redo <card>...                                 merge again a card whose merge conflicted
  ask [<id>...] [--another]                      ask a reader (or one more) to read cards in review
  resume --stream <s> --did <text>               resume a stopped stream, with what was done
  release <sentinel|card>... --reason <text>     release sentinels or held cards
  wait <note> --for <duration>                   park a judgment for a while
  ack <note>[,<note>] --reason <text>            close notes that need nothing done
  answer [--dry-run] [--bar <p>]                 answer the routine judgments through nova-decide

work rows (take, finish, queue):
  queue --as <member|reader> | --stream <s>      a worker's dealt and held cards, or a stream's
  take --as <member> [<card>@<gen>...]           take dealt cards to work on
  progress --as <worker> <card>@<gen>            stamp progress on cards being worked
  finish --as <member> <card>@<gen>              report work done: --head <sha>, or --failed
  stop-return --as <owner-row> <card>@<gen>      hand stopped cards back to their owner row
  lane take <kind> --machine <m> --as <worker>   take a lane on a machine, or queue for one
  lane give <kind> --machine <m> --as <worker>   give a lane or a queue place back
  lane list                                      every machine's lanes and their holders
  budget take <provider/model> --holder <id>     take a rate and concurrency grant for a call
  budget renew <provider/model> --holder <id>    renew the concurrency slot of a long call
  budget release <provider/model> --holder <id>  free the concurrency slot when a call ends
  ci <id>... (--red | --green) --epoch <n>       report a CI run's result on cards
  merge --stream <s> [--red | --conflict <id>]   report a merge's result: red, conflict, landed

reads and review:
  read --as <reader> (--ok | --broken)           record a read's verdict (--begin starts one)
  reads --review [--stream <s>]                  who holds each read of the cards in review

friends:
  friend sync [--root <dir>]                     copy nova-config's friends in; deliver their cards
  collect [<friend>...] [--dead-lanes]           finish friends' cards from their outbox reports
  friend cards <friend> [--json]                 the cards on a friend's row, packets and briefs
  friend up <friend> [--width <n>]               release a friend's hold; --width sets the width
  friend down <friend> [--reason <text>]         hold a friend; the cards stay on the friend's row
  friend hold <friend>... --reason <text>        hold friends; their cards go back to ready
  friend unhold <friend>... [--reason <text>]    release friends' holds
  friend beat <friend> [--working <n>]           a friend's work report, never liveness
  friend take <friend> <id>...                   take cards back from a friend
  friend give <friend> <id>...                   clear a friend's take-back mark on cards
  friend level                                   move queued cards between the friends' rows
  friend stage <card>@<gen> --as friend.<name>   stage a friend's dealt card in a job directory
  friend clean [--days <n>] [--dry-run]          remove friends' finished job directories
  goal set <name> --file <path> [--to <route>]   a person's goal, delivered every 5 running minutes
  goal show [<name>]                             the goals set and their routes
  goal drop <name>                               take a person's goal off

fleet and readers:
  fleet sync [--check]                           make the fleet table match nova-config's machines
  fleet up <member> [--width <n>]                bring a member up at a width
  fleet down <member>                            take a member down; its unfinished work is redealt
  fleet hold <member>... --reason <text>         hold members, whatever they beat (--return too)
  fleet unhold <member>... [--reason <text>]     release members' holds
  fleet quiet <member> --for <duration>          deal a member nothing for a while
  fleet level [--dry-run]                        level members' queues and reads, as the tick does
  fleet beat <member> [--load <percent>]         a member's beat
  hold <name>... --reason <text>                 hold members, readers, friends or streams by name
  unhold <name>... [--reason <text>]             release those holds by name
  reader add <reader>... [--tiers <t,...>]       add readers, up, reading the tiers named
  reader set <reader>... --tiers <t,...>         set the tiers readers read
  reader away <reader>...                        hold readers away, whatever they beat
  reader up <reader>...                          release readers' away hold
  reader retire <reader>...                      retire readers; their reads go to readers up
  reader remove <reader>...                      delete readers holding no read card

routes and cost:
  routes                                         the route table: tier, provider/model, budget, rest
  routes rest <provider|route> --reason <text>   deal no work on a provider or route for a while
  routes wake <provider|route> --reason <text>   end a rest now
  routes limit <provider|route> --rpm <n>        set a model's rate (--concurrent: a provider's)
  funded <provider> --reason <text>              end a provider's rest for funds, once it is paid
  cost reconcile [--dry-run]                     hold today's provider usage against the records
  cost reprice [--since <RFC3339>] [--dry-run]   reprice the records at the routes' current prices
  stats tidy --all --reason <text> [--dry-run]   archive the done counts and count from now
  stats reset --reason <text> | --show           mark the counters; every figure counts from it

landing and releases:
  land [--stream <s>...] [--check <command>]     merge passed cards onto their base and push
  verify-landed [--stream <s>...]                check each landed head is on its base on origin
  landed <id>... --sha <commit> --reason <text>  record a landing git proves (an unreported push)
  merge-window open --for <duration>             pause land while merges are done by hand
  promote [--every <duration>] [--dry-run]       promote landed work toward the development branch
  promoted --sha <merge sha>                     record a promotion
  release check [--window <duration>]            the release's checks: RELEASE OK or NOT READY
  stream set <stream>... [--release <name>]      a stream's release, base, read tier and more
  stream archive <stream>...                     take landed streams off the table
  stream unarchive <stream>...                   put archived streams back on the table
  stream remove <stream>...                      delete streams that hold no card

settings and the seat:
  settings [--json]                              every setting with its value and default
  set [--read-tier <t>] [--attempts <n>] ...     set the sprint's settings
  seat [--repair --reason <text>]                the seat: holder, epoch and generation
  coordinator <name> --reason <text>             move the seat to <name> (or --take, approved)

repair and diagnosis:
  doctor [--all] [--area <group>]                every fault, with its evidence and remedy
  audit [--stream <s>] [--stuck <10m>]           anything blocked, stuck or looped, card by card
  check                                          check the sprint's invariants, each violation
  repair [--dry-run]                             finish a step cut short; re-read under-read merges
  seat check                                     the machinery: server, store, loop, beats, readers
  machinery                                      seat check's other name
  fsck seat [--pg <dsn>]                         whether seat key, record, server and config agree

machines and the store:
  install <server|member|friend-sync|table>      install and load a unit this machine needs
  uninstall <server|member|friend-sync|table>    unload and remove a unit
  units --check [--dir <dir>]                    each unit a sprint needs: there, missing, different
  seat install [--server <host:port>]            record the seat on this machine
  seat uninstall [--dir <dir>]                   remove the retired push loop's unit
  server switch [<binary>] [--rollback]          swap the server binary after a shadow tick
  adopt <version|path> --source <checkout>       roll a build out to the seat through ansible
  live [--json]                                  what is installed and running on this machine
  gc [--machine <m>] [--dry-run]                 remove finished job, read and lander directories
  backup (--out <dir> | --file <path>)           write the store out, checked by a restore
  snapshot --dir <dir> [--keep <n>]              an RDB copy of the store, checked and pruned
  demo load <backup.xz part>...                  load a backup into a throwaway Redis to look at
  demo stop [--dir <dir>]                        stop the demo Redis and remove its directory

help and version:
  help [<verb> | <group> | playbook | all]       this index, or the detail named
  version                                        the version line, with its source commit

detail:
  nova-sprint help <verb>     a verb's whole usage, its flags, examples and exit codes
  nova-sprint help <group>    a group's verbs and words (fleet, friend, reader, stream, lane, goal)
  nova-sprint help playbook   the coordinator's situations, each with its verbs in order
  nova-sprint help all        the full reference: every usage line, the inbox's answers, the words
Every store verb also takes --redis <addr>, --actor <name>, --op <id>, --json and --max <n>.
